title: For Tess
pid: 5efc7b91-fae9-4748-8218-43f008a3cf7a
body: |2-
  Her home note says how to run the suites but not what they cost; the
  measures table under the answer has it now.
  - 'tests/integration/diff-view/test-emacs.el' takes 42 s, a fifth of
    the suite, on any machine; the Neovim one takes 2 s. It calls
    'commit-from-the-message-buffer' twice, and each ends in
    '(skg-test-wait-for-response 20)', whose timeout is ignored: most
    likely both time out every run. Not confirmed.
  - 'bash/all-tests.sh' runs nextest at one job; four jobs took 16 s on
    four efficiency cores, two jobs 26 s.
  - Integration tests edit their fixtures in place, so two sessions'
    suites cannot run at once; over 2026-11-10 to 15 sessions spent at
    least 20 minutes in loops waiting for another session's cargo.
